# Local bookkeeping — these describe the state of Daniel's machine, not the site.
# .canvas-pasted.json records which ?v= he has pasted into Canvas; .build-stamps.json records what
# a build was made FROM. Neither is served, and both would churn the history on every publish.
.canvas-pasted.json
.build-stamps.json
.DS_Store

# Never, under any circumstances. The salt derives every published folder name (site_build.site_salt)
# and lives in class-manager/, outside this tree — this line is the belt to that braces. The
# credential likewise lives one level up, outside the repo, so it cannot be added even by `git add -A`.
.site-salt
github-credential.txt
